{#- _filters.html.j2 — the list filter bar of Korean and every version (list.html.j2, en/list.html.j2; site.js 'list
    filters'). F = present.filter_vm: chips (value, label, n) — the value is the Korean key every version shares, so the
    URL (?type=…&region=…&theme=…&check=1&view=map) means the same in every language; F.w the words
    (locales.LIST_WORDS); [data-result] carries the count line's plural forms (data-forms, {n}) and the 'of all' tail
    (data-of, {m}) for site.js; the '지도 n' count of the list | map switch is the shown rows with coordinates (rows
    data-geo, kept by site.js). Laid out from the first paint with JS, absent without it (the hidden attribute).
    The chips' counts are the whole list's here; site.js turns them into faceted counts as soon as it runs (each chip:
    the rows the list would show with that chip and the other groups' filters), so a chip that would show nothing reads
    0 (outside evaluation 2026-10-18). After the count line, its widest filtered forms (F.widest, .f-w): invisible
    copies that keep the line's width on a desktop, where it sits beside the type chips (css 70-p1), so no chip moves
    when a filter is applied.
    조건으로 찾기 (pipeline/conditions.py, operator 2026-10-31, design ③): where the list has condition chips (F.conds:
    {id, label, n}) they are a row under the type chips and the tools, in the check box's place; they combine (AND), each one's
    count is faceted like the others', ?c=mon,park keeps them (an old ?check=1 is F.legacy), '조건 지우기' at the row's
    end while one is on. The count line keeps its place in the tools (.c-meter): its words stay for a screen reader (the
    live region), the eye reads the count whose digits roll into place, over the ratio bar (aria-hidden; site.js). One
    row more than before, packed tight (a phone's chips are one row it swipes, like the type chips; css/70-p3-conds.css):
    the first results keep their place on the first screen (test_present: 650px desktop, 500px phone). -#}
{% macro result(F) -%}
<p class="f-result" aria-live="polite"><span data-result data-forms="{{ F.forms|tojson_attr }}" data-of="{{ F.w.of }}">{{ F.result }}</span>{% for w in F.widest %}<span class="f-w" aria-hidden="true">{{ w }}</span>{% endfor %}{% if F.conds %}{% set cn = F.cw['count'].split('{n}') %}<span class="c-count" aria-hidden="true">{{ cn[0] }}<b class="c-n" data-c-n>{{ F.count }}</b>{{ cn[1] }} <span class="c-of">{{ F.cw['of']|replace('{m}', F.count|string) }}</span></span>{% endif %}</p>
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro bar(F) -%}
<div class="filters" data-filters hidden>
  <div class="f-top">
    {% if F.types|length > 1 %}
    <div class="f-row f-types" role="group" aria-label="{{ F.w.type }}">
      <button type="button" data-f="type" data-v="" aria-pressed="true">{{ F.w.all }} <span class="tn">{{ F.count }}</span></button>
      {% for v, lab, n in F.types %}<button type="button" data-f="type" data-v="{{ v }}" aria-pressed="false">{{ lab }} <span class="tn">{{ n }}</span></button>{% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="f-tools">
      {% if F.conds %}<div class="c-meter">{{ result(F) }}<span class="c-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i data-c-bar></i></span></div>{% else %}{{ result(F) }}{% endif %}
      <button type="button" class="f-more" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="f-panel" data-f-more>{{ F.w.filters }}<span class="f-badge tn" data-f-badge hidden></span></button>
      {% if F.n_geo %}<div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="{{ F.w.view }}"><button type="button" data-view="list" aria-pressed="true">{{ F.w.list }}</button><button type="button" data-view="map" aria-pressed="false">{{ F.w.map }} <span class="tn">{{ F.n_geo }}</span></button></div>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {% if F.conds %}
  <div class="f-conds" data-conds{% if F.legacy %} data-legacy="{{ F.legacy }}"{% endif %}>
    <div class="f-row c-row" role="group" aria-label="{{ F.cw['group'] }}"><span class="c-lab" aria-hidden="true">{{ F.cw['group'] }}</span>{% for c in F.conds %}<button type="button" data-cond="{{ c.id }}" aria-pressed="false"><span class="c-ck" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ c.label }} <span class="tn">{{ c.n }}</span></button>{% endfor %}<button type="button" class="c-clear" data-c-clear hidden>{{ F.cw['clear'] }}</button></div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="f-panel" id="f-panel" data-f-panel hidden>
    {% if F.regions|length > 1 %}
    <div class="f-row" role="group" aria-label="{{ F.w.area }}">
      <button type="button" data-f="region" data-v="" aria-pressed="true">{{ F.w.all_areas }}</button>
      {% for v, lab, n in F.regions %}<button type="button" data-f="region" data-v="{{ v }}" aria-pressed="false">{{ lab }} <span class="tn">{{ n }}</span></button>{% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if F.themes %}
    <div class="f-row" role="group" aria-label="{{ F.w.theme }}">
      <button type="button" data-f="theme" data-v="" aria-pressed="true">{{ F.w.all_themes }}</button>
      {% for v, lab, n in F.themes %}<button type="button" data-f="theme" data-v="{{ v }}" aria-pressed="false">{{ lab }} <span class="tn">{{ n }}</span></button>{% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if F.check and F.check[1] and not F.conds %}<label class="f-check"><input type="checkbox" data-f="check" value="{{ F.check[0] }}"> {{ F.check[1] }} <span class="tn">{{ F.check[2] }}</span></label>{% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
{%- endmacro %}

{#- the zero-result panel, between the bar and the ledger (so the phone's 지도 view, which hides the ledger, shows it
    too): the sentence, then site.js puts one '<값> 조건 해제' button per filter that brings rows back on its own
    (data-one: {v} = the chip's label in this version) before the reset of every filter. Hidden until nothing matches;
    never shown without JS (the list is then complete). -#}
{% macro zero(F) -%}
<p class="empty" data-empty hidden>{{ F.w.empty }}</p>
<div class="f-undo" data-f-undo data-one="{{ F.w.clear_one }}" hidden><button type="button" data-f-reset>{{ F.w.clear_all }}</button></div>
{%- endmacro %}

{#- after a map's '좌표가 있는 n곳' caption: the places of the page that are not on the map (outside evaluation
    2026-10-18) — n with words.off_map ({n}); site.js keeps it to the shown rows (data-tpl) and hides it at 0. Nothing
    when every place has coordinates. -#}
{% macro off_map(n, words) -%}
{% if n %}<span data-geo-off data-tpl=" · {{ words.off_map }}"> · {{ words.off_map|replace('{n}', n|string) }}</span>{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- the filter keys of one list row (present.list_vm item; en_site.list_vm passes the same keys): empty ones left out;
    data-geo marks a row that is a point of the list map (site.js counts the shown ones: '지도 n', the map caption) -#}
{% macro rec_attrs(it) -%}
{% if it.geo %} data-geo="1"{% endif %}{% if it.tags %} data-types="|{{ it.tags|join('|') }}|"{% endif %} data-region="{{ it.region }}"{% if it.themes %} data-themes="{{ it.themes|join(' ') }}"{% endif %}{% for k, v in it.flags.items() %}{% if v %} data-{{ k }}="1"{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% if it.conds %} data-conds="{{ it.conds|join(' ') }}"{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- the row's '이 조건에 맞는 이유' tags (it.why: {id, label, value, src} per condition it meets — present.list_vm,
    en_site.cond_tags): built hidden; site.js shows the tags of the chosen conditions on the shown rows, each with the
    field's label and value and the source's short name (no date: operator decision 2026-10-09). Never shown without
    JS (no condition can be chosen then). -#}
{% macro why(it) -%}
{% if it.why %}<p class="rec-why" data-why hidden>{% for w in it.why %}<span data-cond="{{ w.id }}" hidden>{% if w.label %}<b>{{ w.label }}</b> {% endif %}{{ w.value }}{% if w.src %} <small>{{ w.src }}</small>{% endif %}</span>{% endfor %}</p>{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
